Subject: [PATCH] Do not redefine clock_gettime on mingw-w64

fastdds supplies its own clock_gettime for Windows because MSVC has none.
mingw-w64 DOES provide it, so on that toolchain the definition collides:

  TimedConditionVariable.cpp:70:5: error: redefinition of
      'int clock_gettime(int, timespec*)'

The file already knows about MinGW -- it selects LL instead of i64 integer
suffixes under MINGW_COMPILER, a macro this project's own CMakeLists defines at
line 409 -- so the guard simply extends that awareness to the function itself.
unix_time is inside the guard because clock_gettime is its only caller.

MSVC is unaffected: MINGW_COMPILER is not defined there and the code is emitted
exactly as before.
---
--- a/src/cpp/utils/TimedConditionVariable.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/TimedConditionVariable.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@
     #define exp9         1000000000i64     //1E+9
     #define w2ux 116444736000000000i64     //1.jan1601 to 1.jan1970
 #endif // ifdef MINGW_COMPILER
+#ifndef MINGW_COMPILER   // mingw-w64 already provides clock_gettime; see the port header
 void unix_time(
         struct timespec* spec)
 {
@@ -89,5 +90,6 @@
     }
     return 0;
 }
+#endif // ifndef MINGW_COMPILER
 
 #endif // if defined(_WIN32)
\ No newline at end of file
